      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "SADAGAAT-USA distinguishes itself through a commitment to radical financial transparency and low-cost operations. In FY2024, the organization reported <cite id=\"2\">revenue of $1,294,453</cite> with zero dollars spent on professional fundraising fees. This efficiency is validated by a <cite id=\"4\">97.5/100 rating from Charity Navigator</cite>. Furthermore, the charity has demonstrated rapid growth, achieving a <cite id=\"15\">3-year revenue CAGR of 67.1%</cite>, indicating strong donor trust and expanding operational capacity to serve crisis-affected communities in Sudan."
      ],
      "summary": "founded in 2002, SADAGAAT-USA is a humanitarian organization dedicated to alleviating poverty in Sudan through critical interventions in <cite id=\"1\">water, feeding, health, and education</cite>. The charity operates with a lean financial model, reporting <cite id=\"2\">$1,294,453 in total revenue</cite> in FY2024 while maintaining an exceptional <cite id=\"3\">98.4% program expense ratio</cite>. This means every dollar donated is directed toward service delivery rather than administrative overhead. The organization holds a <cite id=\"4\">97.5/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>, reflecting high standards of accountability and transparency. Their work specifically targets <cite id=\"5\">vulnerable groups such as the blind</cite> and children excluded from the school system. By focusing on essential infrastructure, such as <cite id=\"6\">water sector projects</cite>, SADAGAAT-USA addresses the root causes of disease and displacement in underserved regions. The charity is <cite id=\"7\">verified as zakat-eligible</cite>, offering a specialized <cite id=\"8\">zakat program</cite> that aligns with Islamic principles of wealth distribution to the poor and needy. While the organization demonstrates high financial efficiency, it faces a <cite id=\"9\">high cost per beneficiary of $2,064.84</cite>, which suggests a focus on intensive, high-impact infrastructure projects rather than broad, low-touch aid. Donors can take confidence in their <cite id=\"10\">Platinum Seal of Transparency</cite>, the highest level of recognition for data sharing in the nonprofit sector.",
